      "cluster_id": 3,
      "headline_hint": "Panama-flagged cargo ship sinks off Odisha coast, triggering major search operation for missing crew",
      "section": "india",
      "batch_position": 0,
      "claim_count": 19,
      "distinct_outlets": 4,
      "source_kinds": {
        "fulltext": 19
      },
      "claims": [
        {
          "id": 29,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "Panama-flagged bulk carrier M.V. Ocean Winner sank in the Bay of Bengal off the coast of Odisha.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/ship-sinks-off-odisha-two-rescued-as-navy-coast-guard-continue-search-for-22-crew-members/article71381540.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "M.V. Ocean Winner had 24 crew members onboard, comprising 20 Chinese nationals, three Myanmarese nationals, and one Bangladeshi national.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/ship-sinks-off-odisha-two-rescued-as-navy-coast-guard-continue-search-for-22-crew-members/article71381540.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "M.V. Ocean Winner departed Paradip Port late on August 20, 2026, carrying iron ore.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/ship-sinks-off-odisha-two-rescued-as-navy-coast-guard-continue-search-for-22-crew-members/article71381540.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "Communication with M.V. Ocean Winner was lost 36 hours after its departure, prompting a search and rescue request to the Maritime Rescue Coordination Centre.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/ship-sinks-off-odisha-two-rescued-as-navy-coast-guard-continue-search-for-22-crew-members/article71381540.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "An Indian Navy P8I surveillance aircraft detected two floating liferafts and an oil slick near the reported position of M.V. Ocean Winner.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/ship-sinks-off-odisha-two-rescued-as-navy-coast-guard-continue-search-for-22-crew-members/article71381540.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "Commercial vessel MT Aisopos rescued two Chinese crew members from liferafts by late evening on August 22, 2026.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/ship-sinks-off-odisha-two-rescued-as-navy-coast-guard-continue-search-for-22-crew-members/article71381540.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "Equasis database records show M.V. Ocean Winner was a 28-year-old vessel built in 1998, measuring 225 metres long and 32.26 metres wide, with a capacity of around 73,000 tonnes.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/ship-sinks-off-odisha-two-rescued-as-navy-coast-guard-continue-search-for-22-crew-members/article71381540.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "An inspection of M.V. Ocean Winner in Chittagong, Bangladesh, in June reported three deficiencies, including one with its magnetic compass.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/ship-sinks-off-odisha-two-rescued-as-navy-coast-guard-continue-search-for-22-crew-members/article71381540.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "M.V. Ocean Winner's current owner is based in Fujian, China, and the vessel is covered by Protection and Indemnity insurance effective from August 1, 2026.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/ship-sinks-off-odisha-two-rescued-as-navy-coast-guard-continue-search-for-22-crew-members/article71381540.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "Union Shipping and Waterways Minister Sarbananda Sonowal confirmed that two survivors were rescued and provided medical care.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/panama-flagged-ship-sinks-off-odisha-2-rescued-search-on-for-22-shipping-minister/articleshow/133442072.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "M.V. Ocean Winner sank approximately 230 to 240 nautical miles off the coast while carrying 72,100 metric tonnes of iron ore.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/panama-flagged-ship-sinks-off-odisha-2-rescued-search-on-for-22-shipping-minister/articleshow/133442072.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "M.V. Ocean Winner departed the Paradip coast at 10:42 pm on August 20, carrying iron ore fines.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/panama-flagged-ship-sinks-off-odisha-2-rescued-search-on-for-22-shipping-minister/articleshow/133442072.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "Initial reports from Indian maritime authorities stated M.V. Ocean Winner was bound for China, while other government information indicated Singapore as its destination.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/panama-flagged-ship-sinks-off-odisha-2-rescued-search-on-for-22-shipping-minister/articleshow/133442072.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "The Andaman & Nicobar Command reported that M.V. Ocean Winner sent a distress alert on Saturday from a position around 300 nautical miles north-northwest of Diglipur.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Livemint",
          "url": "https://www.livemint.com/news/india/panamaflagged-cargo-incident-2-liferafts-oil-slick-detected-2-rescued-search-operation-sank-off-odisha-coast-update-11787485691061.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "Victory Star Group Co Ltd requested search and rescue assistance after communication with M.V. Ocean Winner was lost late on August 22.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Livemint",
          "url": "https://www.livemint.com/news/india/panamaflagged-cargo-incident-2-liferafts-oil-slick-detected-2-rescued-search-operation-sank-off-odisha-coast-update-11787485691061.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "The Indian Coast Guard deployed vessels ICGS Varad, ICGS Anmol, and ICGS Vijit to assist in search operations.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Livemint",
          "url": "https://www.livemint.com/news/india/panamaflagged-cargo-incident-2-liferafts-oil-slick-detected-2-rescued-search-operation-sank-off-odisha-coast-update-11787485691061.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "Coast Guard spokesperson Commandant Amit Uniyal reported that rough sea conditions in the Bay of Bengal were hampering search operations.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Hindustan Times",
          "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/2-rescued-22-missing-after-china-bound-iron-ore-vessel-sinks-off-odisha-coast-101787484142328.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "In September 2009, the Mongolian-flagged bulk carrier MV Black Rose sank near Paradip after developing a hull leak while carrying 23,847 tonnes of iron ore.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "Hindustan Times",
          "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/2-rescued-22-missing-after-china-bound-iron-ore-vessel-sinks-off-odisha-coast-101787484142328.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "cluster_id": 3,
          "text": "In 2009, the MV Asian Forest capsized off Mangalore Port on India's west coast due to cargo liquefaction after loading iron ore fines.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "Hindustan Times",
          "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/2-rescued-22-missing-after-china-bound-iron-ore-vessel-sinks-off-odisha-coast-101787484142328.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        }
      ]
    }
